From 076ef1f6dd8bdfe7b1a83a08ecbb12ecedb2e358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:57:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 157/157] XD Netplay: port 1 can be a controller that becomes a
 GBA for XD multi battles (solo test)

New SI device type 14 (XD Multi, Port 1 only). It is a GC controller until
XD asks for a GBA in socket 1, answers NOREP+RDST until XD unplugs the pad,
then runs an integrated GBA on channel 0 until the battle, a cancel, an
error or a link lost before the battle hands socket 1 back to the pad.
Every switch is decided from XD RAM, SIPOLL, the synced pad sample and
tick-anchored GBA resets, and is logged to gba_detect. Hold X+Y+L+R for 3 s
to leave GBA mode or retry while XD still waits at the socket 1 prompt.

Existing device types behave as before. Savestates keep their format;
multi-battle states need this build. Movie recording cannot start with XD
Multi on port 1, and port 1 cannot switch to it during a movie. Netplay
only gets the config hook for now.
